.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-COPY-OBJECT 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-copy-object \- copy an object to another key or bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm copy-object
.BR \-\-source\-bucket | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-source\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.BR \-\-target\-key | \-K
.I KEY
[\fB\-\-target\-bucket\fR|\fB\-B\fR \fIERN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies an object to another key, in the same bucket or a different one.
.PP
The copy gets its own bytes and its own lifetime: deleting either object
leaves the other intact. It starts out with the source's content type,
checksum and attributes, and is a new object in every other respect - its
own ERN, its own creation time.
.PP
Both buckets are checked against the caller's account and, for a caller
with resource grants, against those grants: reading out of one bucket and
writing into another are separate permissions, and this needs both.
.PP
Unlike a move, this reads and writes the object's bytes, so it costs what
the object is big.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-source\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket the object is in. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-source\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key of the object within that bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-target\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key the copy should have. Required.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-target\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Bucket the copy should be created in. Defaults to the source bucket.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The object was copied. The new object is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, no session, either bucket does not exist or
belongs to another account, the source object does not exist, or
something is already stored at the target key.
.SH EXAMPLES
Keep a copy under a dated key:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm copy-object \e
    --source-bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000::bucket:inbox \e
    --source-key report.csv --target-key archive/2026-09-01-report.csv
.fi
.RE
.PP
Copy into another bucket:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm copy-object \e
    --source-bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000::bucket:inbox \e
    --source-key report.csv \e
    --target-bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000::bucket:archive \e
    --target-key report.csv
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-move-object (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-rename-object (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object (1)
